debloated microduck RL framework

Microduck: ~800 g, 25 cm bipedal robot, 14 Dynamixel XL330 servos.
Stack: mjlab (MuJoCo Warp) + PPO (rsl_rl), 50 Hz policies, ONNX export.
Servos use the BAM XL330 voltage/friction model -- at this scale actuator
fidelity is most of the sim2real gap.
Deployment lives in a separate repo (robotd/robotctl).

CREDIT

All of the robot, the physics and the RL recipes are Pollen Robotics' work:

    upstream    https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck_rl
    the robot   https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck

This is a debloated fork, Apache-2.0 like upstream. It keeps the science and
drops the scaffolding:

- no Hugging Face or wandb in the training path -- tensorboard only, and
  checkpoints stay on the machine that trained them (huggingface_hub survives
  in exactly one place, `uv run publish`, which is opt-in).
- all French comments and messages translated to English.
- every self-explanatory comment and docstring deleted; comments are for facts
  you cannot infer from the code.
- no nested packages: src/mjlab_microduck/robot/microduck/... became a flat
  src/ namespace package (6 levels deep -> 3), one task_<name>.py per env.
- dead code, unused dependencies and stale docs removed.

Track upstream for the authoritative version; come here if you want to read the
whole thing in an afternoon and hack on it.

SETUP

Needs a CUDA GPU, uv, make.

    git clone https://github.com/sueszli/quack && cd quack
    make sync
    make tests

WORKFLOW

    make envs      list tasks
    make smoke     64 envs, 5 iters -- run before every long run
    make train     4096 envs, 6000 iters, ~1-2 h for a usable gait
    make play CKPT=logs/rsl_rl/velocity/<run>/model_3000.pt
    make export CKPT=3000    -> weights/output.onnx, obs normalizer baked in
    make infer     CPU MuJoCo deployment rehearsal

- resume: make train ARGS="--agent.resume True
  --agent.load-checkpoint model_3000.pt"
- headless GPU viewer: make play ... ARGS="--viewer viser" (browser on :8080)
- make targets hardcode Mjlab-Velocity-Flat-MicroDuck; for other tasks:

    uv run train  <TASK> --env.scene.num-envs 4096 --agent.max_iterations 6000
    uv run play   <TASK> --checkpoint-file logs/rsl_rl/<exp>/<run>/model_N.pt
    uv run export <TASK> --checkpoint N

- checkpoints: logs/rsl_rl/<exp>/<run>/, <exp> = the cfg's experiment_name.
  --checkpoint N uses the newest run, --checkpoint-file <path> any run.
- always deploy ONNX from `uv run export`, never a hand-converted checkpoint.

TASKS

  Mjlab-Velocity-{Flat,Rough}-MicroDuck    walking, velocity + head cmds (main)
  Mjlab-VelStand-{Flat,Rough}-MicroDuck    walking + fall recovery
  Mjlab-StandUp-{Flat,Rough}-MicroDuck     stand up, then body-pose control
  Mjlab-SitStand-{Flat,Rough}-MicroDuck    commanded sit <-> stand
  Mjlab-GroundPick-{Flat,Rough}-MicroDuck  touch the ground with the mouth
  Mjlab-BallKick-Flat-MicroDuck            kick a ball forward
  Mjlab-Roulade-Flat-MicroDuck             forward roll, land on feet
  Mjlab-Velocity-Flat-MicroDuck-Rollers    roller-skate velocity tracking
  Mjlab-Velocity-Swizzle-MicroDuck         swizzle skating
  Mjlab-RollerCrouch-Flat-MicroDuck        crouch while gliding on rollers
  Mjlab-RollerSlope-Flat-MicroDuck         glide down slopes on rollers
  Mjlab-RollerStandUp-Flat-MicroDuck       stand up onto the wheels
  Mjlab-Spin-Flat-MicroDuck                spin in place on rollers

Backlash twins: insert `-Backlash` before `MicroDuck` for +-1 deg of gear play
per servo, same obs/action dims (src/task_backlash.py). Not for Roulade,
RollerStandUp, Spin.

DEPLOYMENT REHEARSAL

The runtime hot-swaps policies behind one 61-D obs contract. Rehearse on CPU:

    uv run infer --walking walk.onnx --standing stand.onnx \
        --sitstand sitstand.onnx --roulade roulade.onnx --new-cmd-obs

- keys: velocity commands, G ground pick, Y sit/stand, R roulade, K/L kicks.
- --new-cmd-obs is required for current policies; without it infer builds 51-D
  obs and ONNX Runtime dies with 'invalid dimensions ... Got 51 Expected 61'.
- --debug / --save-csv / --record for sim2real comparisons.
- --no-bam swaps the BAM actuators for the XML PD ones.

PUBLISHING

`uv run publish` uploads policy.onnx + manifest.json + README to the Hugging
Face Hub in the shape the robot daemon loads. Needs `hf auth login` unless
--dry-run.

    uv run publish --task Mjlab-BallKick-Flat-MicroDuck --checkpoint 3000 \
        --repo <user>/microduck-kick --kind episodic --duration-s 4.0
    uv run publish --onnx out.onnx --repo <user>/microduck-flamingo \
        --kind perpetual --unwind-s 1.5
    uv run publish --onnx out.onnx --repo <user>/microduck-my-walk \
        --kind perpetual --slot walk

- --kind episodic: runs for --duration-s, returns to standing.
- --kind perpetual: runs until stopped -- a gait (--slot walk|stand) or a held
  pose (--unwind-s).
- not publishable: GroundPick (phase-driven), SitStand (posture flag) -- the
  daemon owns those.

On the robot:

    sudo robotctl policy add kick <user>/microduck-kick
    sudo robotctl policy add flamingo <user>/microduck-flamingo --hold 5
    sudo robotctl policy load walk <user>/microduck-my-walk
    robotctl robot do kick

CONVENTIONS

- 61-D actor obs, shared by every policy: 48 proprioception + commands
  [twist(3), head_pose(4), body_pose(6)]. Unused slots are zero-padded, never
  removed.
- joints: 0-4 left leg, 5-8 neck/head, 9-13 right leg. Unactuated joints are
  named passive_*; servo selectors use `^(?!passive_).*`.
- ENABLE_* toggles (e.g. ENABLE_SYMMETRY) sit at the top of each cfg file.
- CLAUDE.md holds the env-building workflow and the reward-design rules.
